// GPU class: medium
//
// States a texture edge of 2048 voxels and 16 GB of texture memory. 2048 is the
// hard limit that every known WebGL device holds, so `low`, `medium` and `high`
// differ only by memory.
//
// Use this profile for a device of the middle class. It sits between `gpu/low`
// and `gpu/high`, and it shows that the memory alone moves the point at which a
// volume reduces.
//
// The profile is a stated value and not a measurement. Nothing probes the
// device, so a real device may hold more or less than this profile states.
//
// Load it with `?customization=gpu/medium`.
{
  "bootstrap": {
    "cornerstone.gpuCapabilityProfile": "medium"
  }
}
